{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he took a daughter of Levi.</b> Levi literally, son of Jacob — she is not traced back to him (as a recent descendant). And Scripture juxtaposed the passage of the redeemer to the passage of the enslavement and the exile, to teach that the Holy One, blessed be He, prepared the remedy before the blow. And these 'takings' were not the beginning of the marriage, for Aharon was already born before Mosheh; and what it left unspecified here, it went back and revealed in the section וארא — as it says (Exodus 6:20) ״ויקח עמרם את יוכבד דודתו לו לאשה ותלד לו את אהרן ואת משה״, and there is no earlier and later in the Torah." "<b>But</b> the sense of ויקח is that he brought her back, for he had separated from her because of the decree ״כל הבן הילוד היאורה תשליכוהו״ — 'every son that is born, cast him into the Nile.' And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: Yocheved was 130 years old when she gave birth to Mosheh. How so? Behold, Scripture says ״אשר ילדה אותה ללוי במצרים״ — her birth was in Egypt but her conception was not in Egypt. And Israel were enslaved in Egypt only 210 years. And it is written (Exodus 7:7) ״ומשה בן שמונים שנה״ — 'and Mosheh was eighty years old' — and so on. It follows that when she gave birth to Mosheh she was 130 years old. And the reason Scripture calls her בת — 'daughter' — is that the signs of youth were renewed in her."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:09.377382649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}